MID_EV11_052_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_052_m01_001: Hi, Mom! What's going on? Something good happen?
MID_EV11_052_m01_002: I've received a response from Father about my report\non the incident from the other day.
MID_EV11_052_m01_003: He wrote words of thanks for the resolution of the\nmystery in the temple.
MID_EV11_052_m01_004: It's been a long while since I received any words of\npraise from him.
MID_EV11_052_m01_005: That's good news! Well, I just figured it was about\ntime I returned your spear.
MID_EV11_052_m01_006: As is my duty, I've entrusted it to someone who was\nintegral in solving the mystery of the disappearances.
MID_EV11_052_m01_007: I reported as much to Father... So, it would seem that\nthe spear ought to remain in your excellent care.
MID_EV11_052_m01_008: Really? Thank you! I have to be honest, it does give\nme a lot of confidence.
MID_EV11_052_m01_009: I want to ask you about your demon eye. Have you \nnoticed if anything about it has changed?
MID_EV11_052_m01_010: Actually, ever since we went to Balor's temple, it...\nIt feels like it's been getting stronger.
MID_EV11_052_m01_011: And sometimes...I hear this creepy voice.
MID_EV11_052_m01_012: I've felt more nervous about it too. If it goes on like\nthis, is it going to take over my mind?
MID_EV11_052_m01_013: It reminds me of Inyoni. We fought her in the\nqualifiers, and she said she heard a voice.
MID_EV11_052_m01_014: I might know a way that you can tame that power.
MID_EV11_052_m01_015: I've told you before, but my mother, Yu Phas, kept\nwatch at Balor's temple. 
MID_EV11_052_m01_016: The progenitor god commanded her to appease my\ngrandfather's soul by spending her days in prayer.
MID_EV11_052_m01_017: Cai, I'm going to cast a spell on you. It's a charm my\nmother taught me, once upon a time.
MID_EV11_052_m01_018: Haaah...
MID_EV11_052_m01_019: That's amazing, Mom! I feel like the fog's cleared\nfrom my head! I'm totally refreshed!
MID_EV11_052_m01_020: It seems the evil influence is subdued. You shouldn't\nhave to worry about it, at least for a while.
MID_EV11_052_m01_021: Now, tell me about your involvement in the Heroic\nGames. Will you continue?
MID_EV11_052_m01_022: I've still got some things to work out. But you and\nGrandpa—Solel, I mean...
MID_EV11_052_m01_023: I want the two of you to have the chance to meet\nand talk things out. That's my goal with the games.
MID_EV11_052_m01_024: Thank you, Cai. I'll be supporting you, of course,\nand I expect great things from you.
MID_EV11_053_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_053_m01_001: Cai, only two more battles and we'll have won the\nwhole tournament.
MID_EV11_053_m01_002: Hmm...
MID_EV11_053_m01_003: So, say we win this battle against Theodora's clan.
MID_EV11_053_m01_004: Who will we face in the final match?
MID_EV11_053_m01_005: Bertrand's team and Dietrich's team made it through.
MID_EV11_053_m01_006: So whichever team wins their matchup will be our\nopponents in the finals.
MID_EV11_053_m01_007: Both teams are a little short on mercy. But I guess\nTheodora's no different.
MID_EV11_053_m01_008: About what you'd expect for a final stage, eh? Let's\nall remember that we can't let up until it's over.
MID_EV11_053_m01_009: Cai, are you still worried about something? Is your\nfather's illness on your mind?
MID_EV11_053_m01_025: <NCA>Admit the truth.
MID_EV11_053_m01_026: Honestly, yes. I feel like it's weighing me down.
MID_EV11_053_m01_010: What?! But it's precisely because his time is short\nthat our battles are so important.
MID_EV11_053_m01_011: You, Aurora, and Castor need to be together for as\nlong as possible.
MID_EV11_053_m01_012: Ah... I see your point.
MID_EV11_053_m01_013: Tialla, thank you. You're exactly right.
MID_EV11_053_m01_014: What you just said makes me think of ol' Morrow's\nface the other day.
MID_EV11_053_m01_015: In the 80 years he lost, he grew older than his\nfather, who was trapped in that painting.
MID_EV11_053_m01_016: But even after all that loss, he came out of it smiling.
MID_EV11_053_m01_017: He chose not to cry over what he'd lost, because he\nwas so happy about getting his family back.
MID_EV11_053_m01_018: He said it better himself. He was so positive about all\nof it. Good ol' Morrow.
MID_EV11_053_m01_019: Yeah... That really puts things in focus. I've gotta\nsave Pop.
MID_EV11_053_m01_020: We don't know how much time he has left, but even\nif it's only a little while, I have a job to do.
MID_EV11_053_m01_021: Me, Mom, and Pop—we should be together. We can\nstill have some good times ahead of us.
MID_EV11_053_m01_022: Pop's a weird old guy, but he's my weird old guy.\nWell, mine and Mom's. And he deserves to be happy.
MID_EV11_053_m01_023: Good things are good, no matter how long they last.
MID_EV11_053_m01_024: You've got it just right, Cai.
MID_EV11_084_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_084_m01_001: You have come further than I could have dreamt at\nour first meeting.
MID_EV11_084_m01_002: It is as if you and I have been linked by causality\nsince that moment in the plaza.
MID_EV11_084_m01_003: I've had bigger problems than that lately, but I've\ndecided not to worry about them anymore.
MID_EV11_084_m01_004: I'm sorry, Theodora, but I won't be letting you take\nthe victory today.
MID_EV11_084_m01_005: If victory is decided by conviction alone, then I think\nit shall not be up to you.
MID_EV11_084_m01_006: For I am driven by the long-held dream of more than\na million Saraminians.
MID_EV11_084_m01_007: Hm?
MID_EV11_084_m01_008: What is that spear he wields? I can feel its\nstrangeness from here.
MID_EV11_084_m01_009: It does not look quite like one of Drake's treasures.
MID_EV11_084_m01_010: The temples hold sacred weapons, called Arcs. They\nare powerful artifacts, possessed of special strength.
MID_EV11_084_m01_011: That one, I suspect, is among the greatest of them.\nThey are called Supreme Arcs.
MID_EV11_084_m01_012: These weapons were forged for the use of the\ngods themselves.
MID_EV11_084_m01_013: That is unexpected. How would he have laid hands\non one?
MID_EV11_084_m01_014: This spear? It's not mine. I'm just borrowing it.
MID_EV11_084_m01_015: I can't get into all the details, but...looks like I'll be\nusing it for a little while, at least.
MID_EV11_084_m01_016: Your Majesty, between this and what Alexandra\nbore, the temples may be showing their hand.
MID_EV11_084_m01_017: They would arm a child with such a weapon? All to\nspite Saramis?
MID_EV11_084_m01_018: I had thought of him as a minor irritant, but it\nseems I must revise that view.
MID_EV11_084_m01_019: Mark me, boy. I hereby recognize you as a threat\nto Saramis.
MID_EV11_084_m01_020: And as such, I shall rain my full might upon you.\nLet our battle commence!
MID_EV11_084_m01_021: That weapon... Why does that child have the\nStar Spear of Aurora?
MID_EV11_084_m01_022: This must be the person from her report, the capable\none who was "integral in solving the mystery"...
MID_EV11_084_m01_023: That weapon is not a child's toy. What in the world\nis taking place here?
MID_EV11_084_m01_024: He is quite the mysterious child, sporting the right\neye too. You think so as well, don't you Babbu?
MID_EV11_084_m01_025: The color of his eyes, though... I don't think they\nwere like that before.
MID_EV11_084_m01_026: Their disgusting tint reminds me of her eyes.\nSo much so that I'd like to gouge them right out.
MID_EV11_086_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_086_m01_001: I refuse to accept defeat! Not now!
MID_EV11_086_m01_002: Theodora! What are you doing?!
MID_EV11_086_m01_003: HrraaaAAAUGH!
MID_EV11_086_m01_004: YAAAGH!
MID_EV11_086_m01_005: Hng... Rrgh...
MID_EV11_086_m01_006: Not again! Is this gonna be a repeat of last time?
MID_EV11_086_m01_007: Even worse, I fear. That hideous power radiating\nfrom her...
MID_EV11_086_m01_008: Theodora? This is just like with Zenzele.
MID_EV11_086_m01_009: What happened to Troy's warding chain? We JUST\ngot that thing!
MID_EV11_086_m01_010: Shattered to bits, alas. Whatever protection it\nprovided is gone.
MID_EV11_086_m01_011: That... That's...
MID_EV11_086_m01_012: Tobias! Do something to stop Her Majesty, and do\nit quickly!
MID_EV11_086_m01_013: Heard and understood, Bona.
MID_EV11_086_m01_014: Ack! Urgh... Sorry...she's too much for me.
MID_EV11_086_m01_015: Kill... Everyone in my way... I'll cut you all down!
MID_EV11_086_m01_016: That eye...belongs to me... Return it now!
MID_EV11_086_m01_017: Theodora! Don't give yourself over to that power!\nIt's too dangerous!
MID_EV11_054_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_054_m01_001: Will Theodora be alright? I hope she's started\ncoming around.
MID_EV11_054_m01_002: Ah, hello there. Her Majesty is still resting, but you\nmay wait here until she convalesces.
MID_EV11_054_m01_003: Are you sure?
MID_EV11_054_m01_004: Ohoho. Once she wakes, I have a feeling Her\nMajesty will want to speak to you.
MID_EV11_054_m01_005: The match... What happened?
MID_EV11_054_m01_006: Hey, look who's awake! How you feeling, boss?
MID_EV11_054_m01_007: I have no memory of the battle past a certain point.\nWhat happened to me?
MID_EV11_054_m01_008: You lost, Your Majesty. The boy defeated you.\nOr, seen another way, he saved you.
MID_EV11_054_m01_010: I see. I thought that I prepared myself for this, but it\nis still a bitter pill.
MID_EV11_054_m01_011: Theodora, you were so far gone. Everyone was\nworried about you.
MID_EV11_054_m01_012: Hello, Cai.
MID_EV11_054_m01_013: I hadn't any idea it would go this way. Strange to\nthink the boy I once struck down would save me.
MID_EV11_054_m01_014: You have grown powerful—and the spear is not the\nreason. I can see you've worked hard to get here.
MID_EV11_054_m01_015: Boss, I'm begging you to stop using that arm. You're\nplaying with fire.
MID_EV11_054_m01_016: Will I lose my sanity soon, just as he did?
MID_EV11_054_m01_017: Captive to the arm—addicted to its strength—\nso thoroughly under its control that we are one.
MID_EV11_054_m01_018: I mourn that the long-held dream of Saramis may\nnever see fruition.
MID_EV11_054_m01_019: I just realized, I've never asked about that. What is it\nthat you and your group were fighting for, Theodora?
MID_EV11_054_m01_020: I sought to restore the honor of Yu Phas. We would\nhave made Ahm Lu into a holy land once more.
MID_EV11_054_m01_021: And for that, we needed the temples to approve our\nannexation of Cybele.
MID_EV11_054_m01_022: We have petitioned the Divine Sovereign for\ngenerations, all to no avail.
MID_EV11_054_m01_023: The goddess Yu Phas is unfairly despised throughout\nDagda because they do not understand her.
MID_EV11_054_m01_024: But to us, and the other forest peoples, she is a\ncomforting figure. We owe her a great deal.
MID_EV11_054_m01_025: {SetColor=Gray}All these people... They all love Grandma so much.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV11_054_m01_026: We saw the Heroic Games as an opportunity to gain\nwhat we sought.
MID_EV11_054_m01_027: Had we been victorious, the Divine Sovereign would\nbe forced to accede to our demand.
MID_EV11_054_m01_028: But after this defeat, those hopes are dashed. Again.
MID_EV11_054_m01_029: Yet as queen of Saramis, I will not rest until I make\nour dream real. And if I cannot, my successor shall.
MID_EV11_054_m01_030: You should be proud of the strength you have gained,\nCai. Very few men are capable of defeating me.
MID_EV11_054_m01_031: If my dream could not be fulfilled, I shall pray to\nYu Phas that yours is.